# gitleaks findings that are deliberately not failures. One line per finding,
# each a FINGERPRINT: <commit>:<path>:<ruleID>:<line>.
#
# The rule for what may go in here:
#
#   Anything we introduced, or anything we could remove, must be FIXED — never
#   covered by an entry here. This file is only for a pre-existing fact we
#   neither introduced nor can remove at acceptable cost.
#
# And the shape is load-bearing. Entries are fingerprints and nothing else:
# never a path exclusion, a rule exclusion or a regex. A fingerprint names one
# frozen instance in one commit, so it is a RECORD and cannot grow. A path or a
# rule names a pattern, so it silences that file's or that rule's FUTURE too —
# that is a hole, and the knob added to make the gate usable is exactly the
# knob that turns the gate off.

